    "b-dn-02": {
      "id": "b-dn-02",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A decision node is a specialization of "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kernel.call",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Structured Calls (BAML)",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "90-specs/10-model-nodes/10-structured-calls-baml"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It keeps the same identity (container, session, run, turn) and the same cost path. Its session kind is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "decision",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It has its own input contract, result type, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "decision_made",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " event, and viewer card."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-03": {
      "id": "b-dn-03",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Status: proposal, nothing built. Jev is usable today through early access. The OpenAI Decisions API is not usable yet."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-04": {
      "id": "b-dn-04",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why Not Just a BAML Enum"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-05": {
      "id": "b-dn-05",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A native engine returns a probability for every option. A BAML enum returns one label, and any confidence the model writes into its output is not calibrated."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-06": {
      "id": "b-dn-06",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Aspect",
          "Native engine (Jev)",
          "BAML enum"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Output",
            "A probability per option, from the model itself",
            "One label. Any confidence is text the model wrote"
          ],
          [
            "Many questions",
            "All answered in one parallel pass, nearly free",
            "A longer prompt, or one call per question"
          ],
          [
            "Latency",
            "About 100 ms",
            "Seconds"
          ],
          [
            "Rationale",
            "None",
            "Yes, as a typed field"
          ],
          [
            "Generation",
            "None. Closed answers only",
            "Any typed output"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-07": {
      "id": "b-dn-07",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A native engine is weak in four cases. Handle them before the call, or use the BAML engine:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-08": {
      "id": "b-dn-08",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Arithmetic, counting, and dates. Compute them in code and put the result in the state."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-09": {
      "id": "b-dn-09",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Indirection. A question about a fact several steps removed from the state gets a weak answer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-10": {
      "id": "b-dn-10",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Large, distracting state. Filter the slice down to what the question needs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-11": {
      "id": "b-dn-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Adversarial text. Instructions inside the state can sway the answer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-13": {
      "id": "b-dn-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Engines"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dn-14": {
      "id": "b-dn-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Three engines fit the node contract. Jev and the BAML fallback work today. The OpenAI Decisions API waits on a published endpoint."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
